    a: "<b>Preferred HIV regimen for treatment-naive adults (DHHS Guidelines):</b><br><b>First-line preferred:</b><ul><li><b>Bictegravir/tenofovir alafenamide/emtricitabine (BIC/TAF/FTC — Biktarvy)</b> — once daily, high barrier to resistance, well-tolerated</li><li><b>Dolutegravir/abacavir/lamivudine (DTG/ABC/3TC — Triumeq)</b> — if HLA-B*5701 negative (abacavir hypersensitivity screening)</li><li><b>Dolutegravir + tenofovir (TAF or TDF)/emtricitabine</b></li></ul><b>Drug class summary:</b><ul><li><b>NRTI</b> (nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors): TDF, TAF, FTC, 3TC, ABC — backbone of regimen</li><li><b>INSTI</b> (integrase strand transfer inhibitors): bictegravir, dolutegravir, raltegravir — preferred 3rd drug</li><li><b>NNRTI</b>: efavirenz, rilpivirine — older first-line; rilpivirine needs adequate gastric acid, pill load</li><li><b>PI</b>: darunavir/ritonavir — used in specific scenarios (PI-boosted with ritonavir or cobicistat)</li></ul><b>Goal:</b> Achieve undetectable viral load (&lt;20–50 copies/mL) within 3–6 months."
