    a: "<b>Lithium toxicity:</b><br><b>Signs (by severity):</b><ul><li>Mild (1.5–2.0 mEq/L): nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, <b>fine tremor</b>, polyuria, polydipsia</li><li>Moderate (2.0–2.5): coarse tremor, ataxia, confusion, drowsiness, slurred speech</li><li>Severe (&gt;2.5): seizures, coma, arrhythmias, death</li></ul><b>Risk factors for toxicity:</b><ul><li>NSAIDs (reduce renal clearance), thiazides, ACEi, hyponatremia, dehydration, renal impairment</li></ul><b>Management:</b><ul><li>Stop lithium; IV normal saline to restore euvolemia (lithium follows sodium handling)</li><li>Monitor lithium levels q4–6h</li><li>Mild: IV hydration, supportive care</li><li><b>Hemodialysis for:</b> severe symptoms, lithium &gt;4 mEq/L regardless of symptoms, or &gt;2.5 mEq/L with renal failure or hemodynamic instability</li></ul><b>Long-term effects:</b> <b>Nephrogenic DI</b> (polyuria/polydipsia), hypothyroidism, hyperparathyroidism, renal insufficiency — monitor BMP, TFTs, and levels every 6 months."
