    a: "<b>Special populations — anticoagulation choice:</b><br><b>Antiphospholipid syndrome (APS):</b><ul><li><b>Warfarin preferred</b> — NOACs (especially rivaroxaban) shown inferior to warfarin in triple-positive APS (RAPS, TRAPS trials)</li><li>Target INR 2–3 for VTE; INR 2.5–3.5 for arterial thrombosis/recurrent events</li></ul><b>Cancer-associated thrombosis (CAT):</b><ul><li><b>DOACs preferred</b> for most cancers (edoxaban or rivaroxaban — HOKUSAI-VTE Cancer, SELECT-D trials)</li><li>LMWH (enoxaparin) also acceptable; still preferred for GI/GU malignancies due to higher bleeding risk with DOACs</li></ul><b>Pregnancy:</b><ul><li><b>LMWH (enoxaparin)</b> — safe, does not cross placenta</li><li>Warfarin: teratogenic (embryopathy weeks 6–12, CNS malformations); avoid in first trimester; can use in 2nd trimester for mechanical valves</li><li>NOACs: contraindicated in pregnancy (insufficient data, animal teratogenicity)</li></ul>"
